		<!-- ═══════════ Why files ═══════════ -->
		<section class="band band-dark">
			<div class="wrap center">
				<p class="eyebrow">Why Not Servers?</p>
				<h2 class="h-xl">No servers. No skills lottery. <span class="grad">Just files.</span></h2>
				<p class="sub">
					MCP servers pollute the context window. Skills retrieve probabilistically and drift out
					of sync. Sub-agents add overhead. Files are deterministic — and reading them is a primitive
                    skill every agent already has.
				</p>
				<div class="no-chips">
					<span class="no-chip">✕&nbsp; No MCP servers</span>
					<span class="no-chip">✕&nbsp; No skills lottery</span>
					<span class="no-chip">✕&nbsp; No sub-agents</span>
					<span class="no-chip">✕&nbsp; No API keys</span>
				</div>
				<p class="pull">
					“Don't add infrastructure when the agent's existing capabilities — reading files and
					following references — <span class="grad">already solve the problem.</span>”
				</p>
			</div>
